translations.text:
Great are the eyes, brief the gaze

(or Love shortens it, aiming to wound);

the brow is a bow, the look its arrowhead,

to which Love owes his conquests.


Her cheek owes its pearl to pearl;

where a rose, dead in coral flames,

would be, its fire joins more closely

the lily's tempered snow.


Art is supreme, yet artlessly

genius hits the mark, not by good fortune;

her walk is measure, not care.


She claims no share in so many parts;

she could be beautiful without beauty;

without love, I would have lived in love.
